// Every user-visible string, in every supported language - see i18n.h.
// Included (X-macro style) by i18n.h and i18n.cpp; not a standalone header.
//
// Rules (enforced by tools/check_i18n.py, run in CI):
// - One row per line, one plain "..." literal per column (no literal
//   concatenation), no empty cells.
// - TR rows (e-paper UI): printf specifiers (%s, %u, %d, %lu, %%) must
//   match across columns, in the same order. Only ASCII + U+00C0-U+00FF -
//   the lv_font_it_* fonts carry nothing else (so no oe ligature, no
//   guillemets, no typographic apostrophe, no ellipsis character; use
//   ASCII ' " ... instead). Keep hints short: they wrap onto at most two
//   lines of a 200 px wide screen.
// - TRW rows (web pages): {0}, {1}, ... placeholders must match across
//   columns; any Unicode is fine. The key is what the pages' t("key") and
//   data-i18n="key" attributes use.
//
// Adding a language: add a column to every row, a value to i18n.h's Lang
// and its code/name to i18n.cpp, and an <option> to SETTINGS_HTML.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// E-paper UI
//  id                          en, it, fr
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
